shortCircT -- && AND || EXIT EARLY, BOTH SWITCHES, BOTH ROADS (SEQ 337, 2026-10-12). Measure and pin only.

Intended (the C1 buy, 2026-10-06): when the left operand decides the answer, the right operand does not run; when it does
not decide, the right operand runs exactly once. The mixed line is the strict left fold, (a || b) && c.

The operands X Y a b c are callees that bump their own declared counter (declared, because two actions touch each --
bear-trap 39) and return a value; scF / scT are plain fields holding 0 / 1. Each line prints
    SC <line> <seat> <column> x <X ran> y <Y ran> a <..> b <..> c <..> v <value>
Seats (respelled SEQ 338): A = on the right of `=`; I = the folded condition `if a && b;` (one-statement arm); N = the same
as nested ifs `if a; if b;` (the && lines only -- || has no nested spelling without else); B = an if whose arm is an
indented two-statement body (this seat was "F" in SEQ 337). For the if seats v is 1 when the arm ran.
k1-k4 (SEQ 338) put a CALL on the left, counted in the a column: k1 / k2 return the fields 0 / 1, k3 / k4 return
falseResult / trueResult. k1 / k2 agree on every road -- the call is not the difference. k3 / k4 split by ROAD, both
switches: the node kant's sentinel names resolve to carries no count (fixit falseResultTruthy). The jit seeds it with
jitSeedField, which loads gCount (0) -- both sentinels read FALSE; the interpreted truthOf answers 1 for a non-count -- both
read TRUE. So k3 is wrong interpreted (exprPinT S3's row) and k4 is wrong jitted.
Columns: fire = the testing() run (emit + first fire); jit = jitRefire after a counter reset, so it counts run time only;
int = the interpreted oracle, run last (bear-trap 25). The switch is the environment's INCANT_EXPR_ACCUM.
m1's values are a=1 b=1 c=0, chosen so the two folds disagree on value AND counts: left fold (a||b)&&c reads a1 b0 c1 v0;
right fold a||(b&&c) reads a1 b0 c0 v1.
n1 and n2 are the witness control: X runs once there. If they read 0 the counter is broken and no other row means anything.
